 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Deforestation is the clearing of forest without replacing it. Cameroon's southern forests, part of the Congo basin, are losing trees.\nCauses: logging for timber exports; clearing for farms (shifting cultivation) and plantations (oil palm, rubber, cocoa); cutting firewood and making charcoal; growth of towns and roads; mining; bush fires.\nManifestations (how we see it): shrinking forest areas, fewer large trees, logging roads and timber lorries, bare or eroded land, loss of wildlife (gorillas, elephants), rivers silting up.\nConsequences: soil erosion, loss of biodiversity and medicinal plants, less rain locally, climate change (trees store carbon), loss of livelihoods for forest peoples.\nSolutions: reforestation, controlled and selective logging, national parks (Dja, Lobéké, Korup), improved stoves, agroforestry, education.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "f": "the forest near a village"
  },
  "problem": "Give two causes of deforestation of {f} and one solution.",
  "steps": [
   "Causes: clearing land for farms, and cutting firewood and making charcoal.",
   "Solution: plant new trees and use improved stoves that need less wood."
  ],
  "answer": "Farming and firewood; solution: reforestation and improved stoves.",
  "checks": []
 },
